## When Should You See a Doctor?

Consider speaking with a healthcare professional if you frequently miss periods, experience consistently very heavy bleeding, have severe pelvic pain, bleed between periods, or notice a significant and persistent change in your normal cycle.

Medical advice is particularly important when irregular periods are accompanied by other symptoms.

## Understand Your Normal Pattern

One late period does not necessarily mean something is wrong. Menstrual cycles can change occasionally for many reasons.

The important thing is to understand what is normal for you and recognise when a change becomes persistent.

Tracking your cycle, maintaining healthy lifestyle habits, choosing suitable menstrual products, and seeking professional guidance when necessary can help you manage irregular periods with greater confidence.
